I hope this is not the wrong list to send to :-)
 
With the idea of naming the LAN bridge interface "br-lan" in OpenWrt
kamikaze there are numerous log messages "Warning: wierd character in
interface `br-lan' (No aliases, :, ! or *).".
I don't criticise their naming convention, but everytime I see that message,
I wonder if the typo in that message (should read "weird", see
http://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/weird) is intentional or actually just a typo?

Secondly, there are different type of quoted used (` and '). 
 
